<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajah Salalila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajah Salalila is remembered in tradition as the first ruler of the Bruneian-allied dynasty of Maynila, set up around 1500 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolkiah">Sultan Bolkiah</a> of Brunei is said to have conquered the town. His line, which included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-matanda">Rajah Matanda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-sulayman">Rajah Sulayman</a>, ruled the Muslim port until the Spanish conquest of 1570–1571.</p></div>
